  "raw_text": "old you what my autopilot order was. Agent: You're right, you mentioned the Chick-fil-A chicken sandwich. Could you tell me why that specific item is your default or \"autopilot\" order? Is it because... User: Because it's really good and it's always fairly fresh and I know what it tastes like and it's ready quickly. Agent: Thank you. If you get bored of your usual Chick-fil-A chicken sandwich, what do you switch to? Is it a new flavor, a new chain, a different format like a wrap versus a burger, or a different side or drink? What scratches that itch for something different? User: Usually if I want something else I'll just make something at home Agent: That makes sense. How do other people influence your order, if at all? For example, does group choice, recommendations, convenience for others, or not wanting judgment play a role? Could you give one example? User: It doesn't really ever influence my order unless maybe I'm with someone who specifically doesn't like Chick-fil-A. Agent: Unde",
